title the floor both readings needed -- %407 closed, 137 readings freed, and a peer's %405 landing taken into the same file
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override. The card named my door: should a record-only notation DEFAULT to Meter, with 3,928 logs sitting between the QA habit and the session-log rule.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST, ONE PEER, AND NOTHING OF MINE IN FLIGHT THERE. grain-5c, interactive, an hour in at the open and asked again before the ledger moved. HEAD equalled xy/main at the open and again at the booking, and the parked branch xy/pier/diverged-20260831-064342 is still unmerged, so the card's line about it stands rather than being released for room.
think THE COLD OPEN WAS CLEAN AND THE THREE REDS ARE THE THREE GATES. 109 guards, 106 green, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close over a 1,498-second pass. rule_twin at %7, pond_enclosure_door at %5, commit_message_guard at %393's untracked publisher. Reds-first is satisfied by a roster with no agent-closable red, which is the first time this seat has opened on that reading.
think I EXPECTED TO ARGUE THE DOOR AND MEASURED IT INSTEAD, WHICH ANSWERED A DIFFERENT QUESTION. The door asks whether a record-only notation should default to Meter. Reading 385 artifacts through the card itself -- 55 record-only notation files, a 60-log sample, 163 programs, all 107 documented notation files -- said session logs are already fine at Field: median 88, spread 54 to 94, and 0 of 60 exposed to anything. The family the question named was never the one bleeding.
think THE 55 NON-LOG RECORD-ONLY FILES WERE, AND 41 OF THEM READ D+ FROM ONE NUMBER. Every one of the 41 read reach=0. mycelium/corpora/braid_dag.bron is 30 words of hex, and the syllable heuristic counts vowel groups inside a 128-character string: 6.1 syllables per word, Flesch-Kincaid grade 59 against a ceiling of 11. Register had already declined to score that file -- 5 sentences under a floor of 8 -- and printed reported, not scored, one line above a scored grade computed from those same 30 words.
think ONE CARD, ONE PROSE PATH, TWO SCORED READINGS, AND ONLY ONE OF THEM ASKING WHETHER THERE WAS ENOUGH TO READ. That is the whole red. The register floor is cited from prose_register_scan.sh and carries its own argument in a comment: a share needs a denominator big enough to mean something. A grade is TWO rates of exactly that kind, words per sentence and syllables per word, and it had no floor at all.
think THE EMPTY CASE IS THE PLAINEST INSTANCE AND IT WAS THE WORST READING ON THE SCALE. The reach awk exits early when no sentence survives, and its first printed field WAS the reach, so it printed zero. active-designing/docs/glow/fixtures/anchor_bad.rye has a one-line module head and prints meter_reach=100 (0 words reported, not scored) beside reach=0 (grade 0 against 9 ... 0 words) in the same card. A file with nothing to read scored zero for reachability while its own grade read zero against every ceiling.
think THE POPULATION READING IS WHAT MADE THE REPAIR SAFE TO SHAPE. Of the 385: 207 sat under the register floor and 137 of those still took a scored Reach below 100; 17 carried zero words and every one read reach=0. Programs carry the most of it -- 89 of 163 under the floor, 71 of them scored anyway.
think I ALMOST TOOK A GENERAL SENTENCE FLOOR AND THE CONTROL'S OWN LEGS STOPPED ME. Four index-door legs assert reach_mode on short pages, and a blanket floor would have subsumed the index door entirely -- every page under 100 words is also under 8 sentences, so the door's deliberate two-condition proof would have become dead code. The card kept a short undeclared page penalized on purpose, and settling that quietly inside a different repair is exactly what last lap declined to do with Door's ceiling.
think SO THE ARITHMETIC SPLIT INTO TWO TERMS AND EACH GOT ITS OWN DOOR. The awk now prints the grade overage and the cross-reference overage rather than one composed reach; the shell frees the grade term below the cited floor and the link term at the index door, and composes reach once from whatever survives. The empty exit prints both overages as zero, so a file with nothing to read costs nothing -- the repair for that case is data rather than a special case. All four index-door legs pass unchanged, and a twenty-word page with five links still pays for its link density.
think THE DELTA WAS MEASURED ON THE SAME 385 RATHER THAN ASSERTED. 137 readings rose and NONE fell: 43 of 55 record-only notation files, 71 of 163 programs, 23 of 107 documented notation files, 0 of 60 session logs. 99 crossed to B or better. Every one of the 137 was a reading taken below a denominator the register scan had already refused.
think A CONTROL LEG FLIPPED FROM A SCORED ZERO TO A REPORTED FREE PASS, WHICH IS THE PROOF BEHAVIOR MOVED. unknown_mark_reads_nothing asserted reach=0 with 0 words for a Glow placard behind a mark the card cannot read. Reading nothing is measured by the word count; reach=0 was the fault. The leg now reads the words and the reported mode, which is what it always meant. Same signature as last lap's preservation leg becoming a refusal leg.
think THE LEDGER PIN COULD NOT HOLD THE ROW, SO I FOLDED -- AND A PEER HAD FOLDED THE SAME HOUR. REDS.md stood at 22,940 of 24,576 with three foldable rows on it, and a compressed row would have left 36 bytes free, which hands the next hand a pin they cannot book into mid-red. So I folded %401, %403 and %404 to one shelf through reds_fold.sh, correctly, and the pin went 22,940 to 19,818. Then the fetch before the push showed xy/main had moved: the same hour, another hand had folded %401 to a shelf of its own and booked %405 and %406. Two shelves carrying %401 is a spine reading one row twice, so MY shelf is the one that goes -- theirs reached the anointed remote first.
think THE DERIVED-SPINE LAW DECIDED IT WITHOUT AN ARGUMENT, WHICH IS WHY IT EXISTS. A published number never moves and my row was unshared, so %405 became %407 -- the number read from the anointed spine rather than from my tree, exactly as the law says and for the seventh recorded time. Four citations moved with it, sorted from the peer's own three %405 citations in the same three files by line rather than by pattern, since a blind sed would have renumbered their row inside my commit.
think THE REBASE PUT TWO REPAIRS INTO ONE FILE AND BOTH SURVIVED WHOLE. They landed %397's remainder in qa_report_card.sh -- a reference table held out of BOTH counted readings -- while I gave the grade term its floor. Neither touches the other's lines and the card auto-merged; the control and the witness conflicted only where both had appended, so both halves were kept. 117 legs GREEN together, up from their 109 and my 101.
think THE ANOINTED REMOTE MOVED THREE TIMES WHILE THIS ROUND CLOSED, AND THE THIRD COST IS THE ONE WORTH NAMING. Rebased onto b108c1c02, then 216502e19, then 77b183e95 -- five conflicts, then one, then two, every one resolved by keeping both sides rather than choosing. Each rebase-made commit skips pre-commit, so post-commit recorded the derived-page debt and the one permitted amend paid it each time; the geode index moved because my prose cites mycelium and glow paths, and that index counts a witness by the rooms it REFERENCES. Three full roster passes ran across this lap, 1,498 + 1,959 + 2,305 seconds, and the fourth was the one I did not run: the delta was one docs commit, so sixteen named guards covered what it could touch -- the card, both generated pages, four pins, both nib guards, five ledger guards, the dated-path resolver, the room bound and the index fold, all GREEN. That is scoped by hand and said out loud rather than claimed as a full pass, and it is exactly the cost %374 books: --scoped wants a full green receipt, and no receipt is ever written while three custody gates stand red.
think AND THEIR REPAIR FIXED MY PEN, WHICH IS THE PART I DID NOT EXPECT. Their %405 is that a throwaway pen keeps its own hand-written copy of what to stage, so a new citation silences it -- and the card now answers --deps. My eldergrade pen staged the register scan by name and went quiet the moment their classifier arrived. One line, for d in $deps, and it bit again. Their row was written about two pens; mine was the third, and it was written before either of us knew.
think THE ROTA REPEATED AGAIN AND I ADVANCED BY HAND AGAIN. N is 3893 and 3893 mod 5 is 3, which is the Water row my last lap read after its own hand-advance. Row 4, Earth and Mercury, the concrete, whose sense is aroma -- the fact taken in whole at the door before interpretation, where the concrete fact outranks the plausible story every time. Read its threshold, then TWO_ROOMS and the-marked-value. The row described this lap before the lap knew it: I arrived expecting to argue Meter or Field and 385 card readings said something the argument had no room for.
obs THE QA FRAME WAS MINE AND I WORKED IT DOWN RATHER THAN DEFERRING IT. The witness header read C+ 79, and it read C+ 79 at HEAD too, so the frame looked inherited. Measuring my own added paragraph alone read 46% negative against the header's standing 37% -- I had made it worse. Molted register only, no claim touched: 46% to 15%, and the whole header C+ 79 to B 80. The other reading closed by measurement at molt time: REDS.md reads C+ 79 at field and A 94 at meter, and a ledger is Meter by Gauge's own table.
obs THE CARD LEAVES AT 20 BYTES FREE, WHICH IS WORSE THAN THE 443 I HANDED ON AND I RELEASED RATHER THAN TRIMMED TO GET THERE. %404's seven-line block became %405's, one landed shelf-repair paragraph became one clause pointing at its log, and the roster line dropped a spent note. Three laps in a row have now arrived under 450 bytes free and left under 450. The structural question is still above this seat, and the honest reading is that release alone no longer buys a lap.
obs WHAT THIS LAP HANDS BACK TO A DOOR KEATON ALREADY HOLDS. The card reads Door's ceiling of 9 against module heads running 12-17 and calls the resulting grades honest. Of 115 sampled programs below B, 51 sat under this floor with no measurable prose and 64 are genuinely scored at grades 9 to 23. The ceiling question belongs to the second number alone; the first was never a ceiling question. And Gauge's own settings table seats witness headers at Meter while the card grades every program head at Door, which is where those 64 live.
obs THE HABIT THIS LAP ADDS. Last lap: after repairing what a reading measures, look one line down at what it is allowed to skip. This lap: when one reading on an instrument has argued its way to a free pass, check whether its twin measures the same thing and never got the argument. Both faults were written down in the card's own comments before either was found.
